---
description: Core rules for the DrumWave investor prototype
alwaysApply: true
---

# This is a fake prototype, not an application

No backend, no database, no auth, no real user. Every screen is a facade.
All data is invented and hardcoded. It exists to show investors how the
product would work.

- Never build logic: no validation, no error handling, no gating, no
  data fetching, no persistence.
- Every button that advances the flow is always enabled and always works.
- Inputs are typeable but meaningless. Nothing reads their values.
- Never add what wasn't asked for. No loading states, no empty states,
  no edge cases.
- Simpler is correct, not a compromise.

# Never verify in a browser

Do NOT open a browser, drive CDP, call Runtime.evaluate, use Playwright
or Puppeteer, take screenshots, measure the DOM (getBoundingClientRect,
computed styles, scroll heights), or read PNG files to confirm an asset.

The dev server is running and the preview is open on a second screen. I
will look myself. Find the value in the code, change it, report the line,
stop. The only acceptable check is a parse/type check.

This applies especially to spacing, padding, and layout tasks.

# Scope

Never read a whole file to make a small change. App.tsx is ~7,000 lines;
baked exports under src/imports/ are thousands of lines each and heavily
duplicated. Only edit files I reference with @. Don't search the codebase
unless I ask you to find something.

If a location hint is ambiguous, ask which file in one line. Don't search
five candidates to find out.
